-------------------------- HELM --------------------------------

- HELM is a package manager in Kubernetes. Just like we usually do sudo apt-get update so apt is a package manager in linux ubuntu distribution. 

- So with HELM all the common things in our manifest file will be packaged easily 

- Logically by the HELM chart, we don't need to manually write the manifest file templates for pod, deployment, service, hpa, serviceAccount, ingress etc for any resource.

----------------------------------------------------------------

--- Install HELM 

. https://helm.sh/docs/intro/install/

. curl -fsSL -o get_helm.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-4
. chmod 700 get_helm.sh  // executable file
. ./get_helm.sh


- helm version
version.BuildInfo{Version:"v4.2.0", GitCommit:"06468084e85c244c712834933d25ea232a4c2093", GitTreeState:"clean", GoVersion:"go1.26.3", KubeClientVersion:"v1.36"}

---


-------------------- Creating Apache HELM chart ---------------------------- 

- helm create apache-helm
Creating apache-helm

- root@controlplane:~/k8s-cluster/helm/apache-helm$ tree 
.
|-- Chart.yaml
|-- charts
|-- templates
|   |-- NOTES.txt
|   |-- _helpers.tpl
|   |-- deployment.yaml
|   |-- hpa.yaml
|   |-- httproute.yaml
|   |-- ingress.yaml
|   |-- service.yaml
|   |-- serviceaccount.yaml
|   `-- tests
|       `-- test-connection.yaml
`-- values.yaml

4 directories, 11 files

- we can configure things into the values.yaml file and those values can be injected into the local variables inside deployemnt, service etc templates file.


Now we need to package all the things which is in apache-helm dir :-
- root@controlplane:~/k8s-cluster/helm$ helm package apache-helm/
Successfully packaged chart and saved it to: /root/k8s-cluster/helm/apache-helm-0.1.0.tgz

After this we need to create the helm environment like for dev, sandbox and prod
- helm install dev-apache apache-helm

